'''''Silene acutifolia''''' is a species of [[herb]] native to northwest [[Spain]] as well as central and northern [[Portugal]].<ref name="156738-1">{{Cite POWO|id=156738-1|title=''Silene acutifolia''|access-date=19 May 2022}}</ref> The species is [[polycarpic]]<ref name=":1">{{Cite journal |last=BUIDE |first=MARÍA LUISA |date=2006 |title=Pollination Ecology of ''Silene acutifolia'' (Caryophyllaceae): Floral Traits Variation and Pollinator Attraction |url=https://www.jstor.org/stable/42796046 |journal=Annals of Botany |volume=97 |issue=2 |pages=289–297 |doi=10.1093/aob/mcj032 |jstor=42796046 |pmid=16344265 |issn=0305-7364|pmc=2803363 }}</ref> and usually grows in rocky environments.<ref name=":0" />

==Description==
The [[flower]]s are purplish-pink and [[hypogynous]].<ref name=":2">{{Cite journal |last1=BUIDE |first1=M. L. |last2=GUITIÁN |first2=J. |date=2002-12-01 |title=Breeding System in the Dichogamous Hermaphrodite ''Silene acutifolia'' (Caryophyllaceae) |journal=Annals of Botany |volume=90 |issue=6 |pages=691–699 |doi=10.1093/aob/mcf251 |pmid=12451024 |pmc=4240362 |issn=0305-7364|doi-access=free }}</ref> They are also [[Hermaphrodite|hermaphroditic]] and [[Sequential hermaphroditism|protandrous]], however, the temporal separation between the [[male]] or [[female]] stages is incomplete making [[self-pollination]] possible.<ref name=":0">{{Cite journal |last=Buide |first=Mª Luisa |date=April 2008 |title=Disentangling the causes of intrainflorescence variation in floral traits and fecundity in the hermaphrodite ''Silene acutifolia'' |url=http://doi.wiley.com/10.3732/ajb.95.4.490 |journal=American Journal of Botany |language=en |volume=95 |issue=4 |pages=490–497 |doi=10.3732/ajb.95.4.490|pmid=21632374 |url-access=subscription }}</ref> One study from 2002 suggested this might indicate that the species emerged recently in the genus.<ref name=":2" />

